# Rich, semantic output contracts in the exact L1-L4 order from D5.
definitions={
 'Owner':'Accountable team that resolves defects and approves the stated policy. Role ownership is proposed until a named approver accepts it.',
 'Source':'Evidence locator or explicit design/assumption label. A design choice must never be presented as a measured source fact.',
 'Status':'Current lifecycle or evidence state of this row. Distinguish prepared design, executed PASS/FAIL, NOT RUN, PENDING and out-of-scope.',
 'Evidence':'Specific test result, source locator or artifact that supports this row. A planned test is not executed evidence.',
 'Priority':'Delivery importance. P0 protects a mandatory invariant or release gate; P1 supports core usage; P2 is optional reference coverage.',
 'Definition':'One business meaning for the referenced field or entity, including ownership, grain and scope where applicable.',
 'Nullable':'Whether the SQL column permits NULL. This is distinct from a zero, empty string or a documentary UNKNOWN marker.',
 'Null reason':'The exact lifecycle situation that permits NULL. Required even when the field is non-nullable, where it states Not nullable.',
 'Default':'SQL expression applied on omitted value, or explicit No implicit default. Defaults must not invent unknown business facts.',
 'SQL type':'PostgreSQL physical type including precision, scale or maximum character length where applicable.',
 'Class':'Public, Internal, Personal or Sensitive as defined in D1. Sensitive storage requires the documented tokenization/encryption treatment.',
 'Classification':'Sensitivity class that determines permitted access, audit, masking, retention and erasure handling.',
 'Retention':'Proposed purpose-based retention or approved expiry trigger. Legal/finance obligations and holds require privacy-owner confirmation.',
 'Rule IDs':'Existing business/data rule identifiers governing this item. Delimited references in documents are resolved by ID, not copied as database lists.',
 'Expected':'Observable result or value established before executing the stated test at its declared layer.',
 'Actual':'Observed result from execution, or explicit pending/not-run statement. Never substitute a design intention for an observation.',
 'Result':'PASS only if expected and actual agree at the stated execution layer. FAIL exposes a difference; NOT RUN has no observed result.',
 'Target':'Numerical or observable acceptance threshold with unit and workload. Proposed thresholds require owner confirmation.',
 'Unit':'Measurement unit belonging to the target and observed value, such as milliseconds, records, users or ratio.',
 'Target or disposition':'Existing table.column destination, TRANSPORT_ONLY for ephemeral data, or REFERENCE_ONLY for optional attributed external data.',
 'Transformation and validation':'Deterministic conversion plus reject conditions applied before committing the target field. Preserve NULL, units and precision.',
 'Conflict ownership':'Source of truth per field, cutover condition and conflict resolution. User-owned changes cannot be silently overwritten.',
 'Foreign key target':'Referenced table.column enforced by FK, or explicit No foreign key for a scalar field.',
 'On update':'Database referential action on parent-key changes. RESTRICT preserves immutable surrogate linkage.',
 'On delete':'Database referential action on parent deletion. Deletion jobs follow documented child-first retention order.',
 'Source path':'Exact JSON field location in the declared source schema. Each declared field receives exactly one mapping row.',
 'Required':'Whether the source contract requires a field to be present. An optional JSON null is preserved separately from absence.',
 'Direction':'Inbound source to Talentra or Outbound Talentra to provider. Bidirectional exchanges are separate contracts.',
 'Schema SHA256':'SHA256 digest of the saved canonical contract file, enabling deployment-time compatibility verification.',
 'Version':'Contract/model revision. Preserve historical v1/v2 snapshots and use v3 as the current design.',
 'Reason':'Business or engineering justification for this design choice, including the risk addressed and its evidence boundary.',
 'Acceptance':'Specific observable condition that demonstrates the requirement or capability works at the stated layer.',
 'Enforcement':'Database constraint, trusted transaction, API boundary or pipeline that must reject violating behaviour.',
 'Validation':'Type/domain/range, reference and cross-field checks required before accepting this value.',
 'Statement':'Atomic requirement or invariant expressed as observable product behaviour with explicit scope.',
 'Boundary ID':'Stable INT-01 through INT-09 reference to a D1 external-system boundary.',
 'Contract ID':'Stable CON-nnn identifier linking an exchange to its field mappings and JSON Schema.',
 'Mapping ID':'Unique MAP-nnnn identifier for one declared source field and its target/disposition.',
 'Proof boundary':'Execution environment and limits of the evidence. Portable structural checks do not establish native concurrency or target-volume capacity.'}
def meaning(col,section):
 if col in definitions:return definitions[col]
 if col.endswith(' ID') or col in ['Attribute ID','Entity ID','Relationship ID','Operation ID','Gate ID']:return 'Stable '+col.lower()+' used to join '+section+' to its owning requirement, model or test records. Preserve the identifier across revisions.'
 if col in ['Table','Child table','Child','Parent','Parent table','Entity','Objects','Applies to']:return 'Exact singular snake_case physical object or explicitly named logical entity covered by this '+section.lower()+' record.'
 if col in ['Column','Foreign key']:return 'Exact snake_case column name within the named table. Its type and relationships resolve through the current data dictionary.'
 if col in ['Actor','Actor ID','Stakeholders']:return 'Human or system principal whose permitted action and authenticated ownership scope govern this '+section.lower()+' record.'
 if 'rows' in col.lower() or col in ['Candidates','Jobs','Applications','Field count','Active users','Proposed API replicas']:return 'Non-negative count for '+col.lower()+'. Planning volumes are assumptions until measured; counts must use the stated grain and dataset.'
 if any(x in col.lower() for x in ['score','rating','weight']):return 'Numerical '+col.lower()+' evaluated using the disclosed scorecard and evidence. Unassessed review dimensions remain zero.'
 if any(x in col.lower() for x in ['time','date','at','window']) and col in ['As of','Run date','Date','Timestamp']:return 'Calendar/UTC date of the '+section.lower()+' record. The date identifies evidence freshness and does not imply a successful test.'
 return col+' records the '+col.lower()+' needed to evaluate '+section.lower()+'. Read it with the row identifier, owner, linked source and declared proof layer; unresolved values stay explicitly pending.'
